# Implementation Roadmap

A phased approach to building the Fraylon Hackathon Management System.

## Phase 1: Foundation & RBAC (Day 1)
- [ ] Refactor folder structure as per the blueprint.
- [ ] Initialize Firestore collections (`users`, `teams`, `submissions`, `scores`).
- [ ] Update [App.jsx](file:///d:/Visual%20Studio%20Code/Projects/hackathon/HackOS/src/App.jsx) with Role-Based Routing.
- [ ] Create `ProtectedRoute` and `AuthContext` with role fetching.
- [ ] Deploy initial Security Rules.

## Phase 2: Public Interface (Day 2)
- [ ] Build `LandingPage` with Hero, Rules, and Prizes.
- [ ] Implement `LeaderboardPage` with real-time Firestore listeners.
- [ ] Setup `Navbar` with dynamic links based on Auth state.

## Phase 3: Participant Dashboard (Day 3-4)
- [ ] Implement Team Profile view.
- [ ] Build `PaymentUpload` with Firebase Storage integration.
- [ ] Build `SubmissionForm` with GitHub API validation.
- [ ] Add deadline locking logic.

## Phase 4: Admin & Judge Dashboards (Day 5-6)
- [ ] Build Admin `TeamManager` with filtering and status updates.
- [ ] Implement Admin `PaymentReviewModal`.
- [ ] Build Judge `ScoringPanel` with criteria sliders/inputs.
- [ ] Implement auto-aggregation of scores into `teams` collection.

## Phase 5: Polishing & Deployment (Day 7)
- [ ] Conduct end-to-end testing of the round transition logic.
- [ ] Final UI/UX polish (premium dark mode, glassmorphism).
- [ ] Set environment variables and deploy to Firebase Hosting.
- [ ] Handover documentation.
